2.explanation:
The heart of the issue is in List.getPictureCardList (defined in src/upload/list.jsx). This method checks for an itemRender prop and, if present, uses the user’s custom render exclusively: 

    if (typeof itemRender === 'function') {
      item = itemRender(file);
    } else {
      // default markup including delete icon
    }

Because the custom itemRender completely replaces the default markup, the built-in delete icon (the ashbin close control wired to handleClose) never gets rendered. In src/upload/card.jsx the Card component simply passes its itemRender prop down into List, so no further logic intercepts or augments that output. To restore the delete functionality, List.getPictureCardList must merge or append the default close control into the custom render output rather than discarding it entirely.
